              "type": "text",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "content": "OVERVIEW OF THE CELL CYCLE 1027  "
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "content": "The Eukaryotic Cell Cycle Usually Consists of Four Phases 1028  "
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "content": "Cell-Cycle Control Is Similar in All Eukaryotes 1030  "
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "content": "Cell-Cycle Progression Can Be Studied in Various Ways 1030  "
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "content": "Summary 1031  "
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "content": "THE CELL-CYCLE CONTROL SYSTEM 1031  "
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "content": "The Cell-Cycle Control System Triggers the Major Events of the Cell Cycle 1032  "
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "content": "The Cell-Cycle Control System Depends on Cyclically Activated Cyclin-dependent Protein Kinases 1033  "
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "content": "Protein Phosphatases Reverse the Effects of Cdks 1035  "
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "content": "Hundreds of Cdk Substrates Are Phosphorylated in a Defined Order 1035  "
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "content": "Positive Feedback Generates the Switchlike Behavior of Cell-Cycle Transitions 1036  "
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "content": "The Anaphase-promoting Complex/Cyclosome (APC/C) Triggers the Metaphase-to-Anaphase Transition 1038  "
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "content": "The G"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "content": "1",
                  "styles": [
                    "subscript"
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "content": " Phase Is a Stable State of Cdk Inactivity 1040  "
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "content": "The Cell-Cycle Control System Functions as a Linked Series of Biochemical Switches 1041  "
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": [
